The '''2026 Winter Adonia Games''' are an upcoming international winter multi-sport event scheduled to be held in [[Moriya]], [[Nakamizu]], in August 2026. The Games are the flagship winter sporting event of the Adonian sporting calendar and are expected to bring together athletes from across Adonia for competitions in snow and ice disciplines.

The selection of Moriya as host city placed the event in the northern part of Nakamizu, where winter sports infrastructure and mountain venues are concentrated. The August schedule reflects the conventions of the Adonian calendar rather than the southern hemisphere seasons used in some real-world sporting calendars.

== Organisation ==

Preparations for the 2026 Winter Games have centred on venue development, transportation links, accommodation capacity, and broadcasting arrangements. Local organisers have promoted the Games as a major opportunity for Nakamizu to showcase its winter tourism industry and its capacity to host large international sporting events.

== Venues ==

Planned competition venues are expected to include facilities in and around Moriya, with events likely to be distributed between indoor ice venues and nearby mountain sites for snow disciplines.

== Sports ==

The programme is expected to include core winter disciplines such as skiing, skating, snowboarding, and ice hockey, along with other sports approved by the organising committee.

